Now we are going to add: 
scroll animations. Elements fade and slide in as the visitor scrolls down to them.

This one is different from everything so far, because there is no new schema setting. 
The reference uses settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll, 
which is settings, not section.settings

It's a global theme setting (Theme settings → Animations), 
shared by every section, 
so the merchant turns it on once for the whole store. Your section only reads it.

You need to:
1. Add the animation classes to your heading and description. 
Use the same {% if %} inside a class attribute that you already use for full_width:

2. Add the cascade effect to each product <li>. 
This makes the cards appear one after another instead of all at once:

3. Add it to the View all wrapper:





<div class="featured-collection__view-all 
{% if settings.animations_reveal_on_scroll %} scroll-trigger animate--slide-in {% endif %}">

We have a base class, featured-collection__view-all. 
If the "Reveal sections on scroll" animation is selected in the theme settings, 
the scroll-trigger and animate--slide-in classes will automatically activate.
Both of these are global Shopify Dawn classes found in assets/component-animations.css:

.scroll-trigger: This class prepares the HTML element to be animated. 
It acts as the starting point, hiding the element by forcing its opacity to 0 
so it is invisible when the page first loads.

.animate--slide-in: This defines how the element moves. 
It writes a CSS @keyframes instruction that tells the element to start a few pixels lower down the page 
and slowly drift upwards into its final position.




{% endcomment %}





